Track 1: Annealing the Main Duct
- Story & Context: Deep in Level 9 of the San Judas shaft, Mateo Cruz tasted the acrid copper tang of a blown ventilation gasket just as the emergency shutoff sirens cut the main power grid. Instead of letting his crew succumb to the choking blackdamp, Mateo hoisted a rusted twelve-pound sledge and cracked out an explosive 3-2 clave against the groaning air duct, transforming impending panic into a deafening, rhythmic trance that kept forty miners conscious until the rescue cage descended. His hoarse voice tore through the dust-choked darkness with the rallying cry, "Breathe through the seam, let the pipe take the strike."
